===Etymology 1===
{{suffix|urbane|ity}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|urbanit|ies}}

# [[behaviour|Behaviour]] that is [[polished]], [[refined]], [[courteous]].
#* '''1825''', [[w:Washington Irving|Washington Irving]], "[[s:The Crayon Papers/Paris at the Restoration|Paris at the Restoration]]", ''The Crayon Papers'',
#*: The vaunted courtesy of the old school, the smooth '''urbanity''' that prevailed in former days {{...}}
#*{{quote-book|year=1963|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}|title={{w|The China Governess}}
|chapter=9|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W
|passage=Eustace gaped at him in amazement. When his '''urbanity''' dropped away from him, as now, he had an innocence of expression which was almost infantile. It was as if the world had never touched him at all.}}
# {{context|in the plural|lang=en}} [[courtesies|Courtesies]].
#* '''1864''', [[w:Sheridan Le Fanu|Sheridan Le Fanu]], ''Wylder's Hand'', [[s:Wylder's Hand/Chapter XLVII|Chapter XLVII]],
#*: Wealdon's two little visits explained perfectly the active '''urbanities''' of Captain Stanley Lake.

